WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.959
Canada is the sixteenth-largest arms exporter in the world.

00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:07.988
Three point eight billion dollars in annual military exports.

00:00:07.988 --> 00:00:16.102
The Saudi Arabia LAV 6.0 deal — fifteen billion dollars — is the largest arms export contract in Canadian history.

00:00:16.102 --> 00:00:19.204
Nine hundred and twenty-eight armoured vehicles.

00:00:19.204 --> 00:00:27.818
Three hundred and seventy-seven thousand deaths in Yemen — the United Nations' 2022 estimate, including indirect deaths from starvation and disease.

00:00:27.818 --> 00:00:32.306
Twenty-three point four million Yemenis in need of humanitarian assistance.

00:00:32.306 --> 00:00:35.397
Four point five million internally displaced.

00:00:35.397 --> 00:00:38.534
Canadian-made vehicles deployed in that conflict.

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:42.113
Stephen Harper signed the deal in 2014.

00:00:42.113 --> 00:00:47.477
Justin Trudeau refused to cancel it, citing ten billion dollars in estimated penalties.

00:00:47.477 --> 00:00:54.590
Canada ratified the Arms Trade Treaty in 2019, which requires a substantial risk test before export.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.920
Saudi deliveries continued.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.954
The treaty was signed.

00:00:58.954 --> 00:01:00.931
The treaty was broken.

00:01:00.931 --> 00:01:02.818
The weapons were shipped.
